{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew","id":921821,"title":"2E Lodges - Conversions and Homebrew","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-26T19:39:13-07:00","id":921821,"title":"2E Lodges - Conversions and Homebrew","content":"Starting this because I haven't seen any thread yet for people to post ideas for converting 1E Lodges, as well as creating Homebrew ones.<br /> <br /> To start it off, I'm trying on creating a Lodge which has the Eater of Names (Firstborn mentioned from Dark Eras' Sundered World chapter) as its Totem. In terms of size, it's probably big enough to almost rival the Tribal Pillars. And I've been thinking of giving Lodge members access to Lodge Sorcery, and perhaps Lodge Lorehouse as well in addition to a Merit which gives them an extra advantage in devouring <i>Awakened</i> flesh for Essence.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions for what sort of Influences the Eater of Names might have? It's a Rank 5 spirit with possibly two extra Influence dots due to the Lodge's size. Not to mention some Numina slots have been used for five more Influence dots.<br /> <br /> I'm also interested in hearing what additional/alternative Lodge benefits could be given to werewolves under the Firstborn's purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 06-27-2016, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T04:12:25-07:00","id":921931,"title":"","content":"A hint: The Eater of Names is called that for a reason. She didn't hunt mages for no reason. Take a gander at how names affect sympathetic magic etc for a starting point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T07:12:30-07:00","id":921986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=921931#post921931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A hint: The Eater of Names is called that for a reason. She didn't hunt mages for no reason. Take a gander at how names affect sympathetic magic etc for a starting point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah.<br /> <br /> Well, that clarifies things a little bit. So, am I right to assume that she hunted Mages to gain power over them through their true names?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T10:00:51-07:00","id":922064,"title":"","content":"Maybe their Sacred Hunt could allow them to track someone using their Sympathetic Name/Nimbus as a scent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T16:42:40-07:00","id":922285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=922064#post922064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe their Sacred Hunt could allow them to track someone using their Sympathetic Name/Nimbus as a scent?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a good idea.<br /> <br /> Just need to clarify something, though. The Lodge Blessings are entirely separate from the Sacred Hunt benefits, right? Last time I read the Lodge write-ups, there wasn't anything that mentioned what their <i>Siskur-Dah</i> benefits were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T16:44:11-07:00","id":922289,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there is a Blessing, a Ban, an Aspiration and a lodge specific Sacred Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T16:51:00-07:00","id":922293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=922289#post922289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there is a Blessing, a Ban, an Aspiration and a lodge specific Sacred Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, seeing as Acro's little tidbit gave me a better idea on the Eater of Names' concept, I have to post my proposed Blessing to see if it's apt. As for the Sacred Hunt, perhaps I'll go with ZealousChristian's idea that the Sympathetic Name might allow them to track the Mage <i>anywhere</i> for as long as the Condition is active.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Werewolves of the Lodge can use their spirit senses to perceive an Awakened Mage's Nimbus, and can use it to track him down. <br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> Initially, I was also going to add a bonus to tracking rolls involving a Mage's Gnosis. But I wasn't sure how to handle it, especially since I'm not sure what the benefits to tasting the blood of prey are, if any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T16:57:09-07:00","id":922296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=922293#post922293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Initially, I was also going to add a bonus to tracking rolls involving a Mage's Gnosis. But I wasn't sure how to handle it, especially since I'm not sure what the benefits to tasting the blood of prey are, if any.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you've tasted a creature's blood you can sense their direction, no matter the distance or barrier. It lasts a month, or until the werewolf tastes another creature's blood.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest being able to sense sympathetic connections with the target for a sacred hunt blessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T17:12:51-07:00","id":922301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=922296#post922296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you've tasted a creature's blood you can sense their direction, no matter the distance or barrier. It lasts a month, or until the werewolf tastes another creature's blood.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest being able to sense sympathetic connections with the target for a sacred hunt blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about this? Also, I'm going to need a good name for the Lodge. Letting them take the name of their Totem seems less appealing, now.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Werewolves of the Lodge can use their spirit senses to perceive an Awakened Mage's Nimbus, and can use it to track him down. Furthermore, if subjected to a given Mage's Nimbus Tilt, they are treated as having tasted the Mage's blood for the purpose of tracking him. This benefit lasts for a month, or until the werewolf is exposed to another Awakened Nimbus Tilt.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Sacred Hunt</b></u><br /> The Sacred Hunt of the Lodge allows them to detect on sight the sympathetic connections of their prey, as well as determine the nature of such connections. If magic has been used to conceal or falsify a given link, a werewolf may roll Wits + Primal Urge in a Clash of Wills to pierce this occlusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T03:24:24-07:00","id":926960,"title":"","content":"Update on that Lodge idea using the Eater of Names as its Totem. <hr /><br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The adherent of the Lodge can use spirit senses to perceive sympathetic links, and rolls Wits + Primal Urge to scrutinize them. If he uses a given link to track someone, he is considered to have spoor equal to its Withstand rating.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To learn a Mage's sympathetic name.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> To perform a service for whoever offers the adherent his true name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 07-06-2016, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T04:02:26-07:00","id":926972,"title":"","content":"I'd argue one of the first things one sworn to the Eater of Names would be to offer it to be feasted on. Good luck trying to cast sympathetically on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T04:26:13-07:00","id":926983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=926960#post926960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ban:</b> To obey whoever speaks one's true name.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a crippling ban, especially since all of the big three have ways to figure out your true name just by looking at you. Since the Eater is a Firstborn, you could take a cue from one of the bans from the other Firstborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-06-2016, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T04:41:46-07:00","id":926989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=926983#post926983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a crippling ban, especially since all of the big three have ways to figure out your true name just by looking at you. Since the Eater is a Firstborn, you could take a cue from one of the bans from the other Firstborn.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about &quot;To fulfill any oaths sworn on one's true name&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T09:14:26-07:00","id":927117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=926983#post926983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a crippling ban, especially since all of the big three have ways to figure out your true name just by looking at you. Since the Eater is a Firstborn, you could take a cue from one of the bans from the other Firstborn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed, though to be fair you could have a lodge rite or custom that shields one's name from magical detection. Maybe the name is eaten by the totem, or otherwise guarded somehow and can only be discovered via mundane sources? Or admission. Or who knows. Just an idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T09:19:47-07:00","id":927122,"title":"","content":"What about offering a service to one who offers <i>their</i> True Name? Need something done, and you can go to an Eater of Names. Just be aware that they practically <i>own</i> you from that point forward (due to you just handing them a sympathetic connection right to you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-06-2016, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T15:07:58-07:00","id":927295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=927122#post927122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about offering a service to one who offers <i>their</i> True Name? Need something done, and you can go to an Eater of Names. Just be aware that they practically <i>own</i> you from that point forward (due to you just handing them a sympathetic connection right to you).</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Maybe I could pair the Ban and Aspiration to complement one another, and revise the latter as &quot;To learn another's true name&quot;. Or should I strictly limit the Aspiration to the true names of Mages? Either way, revised the Ban in the relevant post.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=927117#post927117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed, though to be fair you could have a lodge rite or custom that shields one's name from magical detection. Maybe the name is eaten by the totem, or otherwise guarded somehow and can only be discovered via mundane sources? Or admission. Or who knows. Just an idea</div> </div> </div> </div>A rite seems like it would make sense. And in addition to shielding one's name from magical detection, perhaps it also somehow extends that protection (in a limited form) to mundane sources? I might need help writing it out, but would it be a Wolf Rite or a Pack Rite for starters?<br /> <br /> Also, I'm going to be giving the Eaters of Names (<i>really</i> need a better name for them) access to the Lodge Lorehouse and Lodge Sorcery Merits, with a choice between Fear, Names, and Punishment(?) for the latter. And how about the Lodge's size? Would it be a moderately big one, or approaching the Tribal Pillars in that aspect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T17:08:44-07:00","id":927359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=927295#post927295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. Maybe I could pair the Ban and Aspiration to complement one another, and revise the latter as &quot;To learn another's true name&quot;. Or should I strictly limit the Aspiration to the true names of Mages? Either way, revised the Ban in the relevant post.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A rite seems like it would make sense. And in addition to shielding one's name from magical detection, perhaps it also somehow extends that protection (in a limited form) to mundane sources? I might need help writing it out, but would it be a Wolf Rite or a Pack Rite for starters?<br /> <br /> Also, I'm going to be giving the Eaters of Names (<i>really</i> need a better name for them) access to the Lodge Lorehouse and Lodge Sorcery Merits, with a choice between Fear, Names, and Punishment(?) for the latter. And how about the Lodge's size? Would it be a moderately big one, or approaching the Tribal Pillars in that aspect?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it locks down use of one's True/Sympathetic Name, maybe a Wolf Rite, with duration, extent, or protection uses determined by Essence spent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T18:10:55-07:00","id":927378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=927359#post927359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it locks down use of one's True/Sympathetic Name, maybe a Wolf Rite, with duration, extent, or protection uses determined by Essence spent?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds about right. Now, for working out <i>those</i> details. I'd say the rite's duration should last a (lunar) month, and the protection should be determined by the amount of Essence spent. Not sure, though, whether it's confined to affecting one target only, or it can somehow be used to include multiple ones (perhaps at a penalty?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T19:03:25-07:00","id":927395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=927378#post927378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds about right. Now, for working out <i>those</i> details. I'd say the rite's duration should last a (lunar) month, and the protection should be determined by the amount of Essence spent. Not sure, though, whether it's confined to affecting one target only, or it can somehow be used to include multiple ones (perhaps at a penalty?).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say one target, but it's a full block on that target (you can't use sympathetic magic upon them or through them). You can always perform the Rite for other targets (which would get expensive in Essence, but that's what comprehensive protected costs).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T22:21:05-07:00","id":927450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=927395#post927395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say one target, but it's a full block on that target (you can't use sympathetic magic upon them or through them). You can always perform the Rite for other targets (which would get expensive in Essence, but that's what comprehensive protected costs).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Here's a tentative write-up...<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Hallowed Name</u> (oo, Wolf Rite)</b><br /> The Lodge recognizes the power to be found in knowing one's name, and that people are connected to the wider world by the abstract ties forged over the course of their lives. They also are aware that witches with the right knowledge can exploit those connections to work their magic upon a person, or those close to him. This rite is performed to hinder such tampering.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Connections, True Name, Warding<br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (20 Successes, each roll represents 5 minutes)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Month<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> For the duration of the rite, any attempt by a character to cast sympathetic magic on or through the targeted character fails unless she spends a Willpower point, or knows his sympathetic name. Even then, this triggers a Clash of Wills, with the werewolf rolling Primal Urge + dots in his highest Renown with the 8-again rule. At Storyteller Discretion, the effects can apply not only to Awakened spells, but also other forms of ritual magic like Blood Sorcery and werewolf rites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 07-07-2016, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T07:58:22-07:00","id":928132,"title":"","content":"What about a higher dot Rite that outright <i>feeds</i> the True Name to the Eater of Names? Target looses all Sympathetic Connections, and what not having those connections would imply (people you were close to treat you like a stranger, identifying information vanishes, etc.). It might be used to punish individuals, or sever them from their old life (so as to serve the Lodge better). They become the person with no name.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://cdn.meme.am/images/298x/15164737.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> &quot;A Wolf has no name.&quot;<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-08-2016, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T08:20:11-07:00","id":928148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=928132#post928132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a higher dot Rite that outright <i>feeds</i> the True Name to the Eater of Names? Target looses all Sympathetic Connections, and what not having those connections would imply (people you were close to treat you like a stranger, identifying information vanishes, etc.). It might be used to punish individuals, or sever them from their old life (so as to serve the Lodge better). They become the person with no name.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://cdn.meme.am/images/298x/15164737.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> &quot;A Wolf has no name.&quot;<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><i>That</i> is scary. And the Game of Thrones reference is a nice one. Now, I am starting to imagine the Lodge being like some sort of Werewolf Faceless Men thanks to it.<br /> <br /> In terms of dot rating, perhaps that Rite would be a five-dot one? I can see it being used effectively as a form of punishment against those who offended/harmed the Lodge in some manner. And it definitely would reinforce the significance of its adherents collecting the True Names of others, including the Awakened who are their sacred prey. Not to mention emphasize how steep a price one must pay to call on their services. <br /> <br /> On a similar note, the Rite would most certainly be the greatest act of devotion that true faithful of <i>Humuz-Ur</i> could demonstrate. And such werewolves are perhaps merely extensions of their Totem's will as well as her favored vessels once they've made that sacrifice. It could be even possible that we could design a lesser Rite that could somehow harness the True Names given to the Firstborn, which could function similarly to the Masque Merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T08:27:27-07:00","id":928155,"title":"","content":"I like that too. Was hard thinking of something that might be appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T09:04:07-07:00","id":928182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=928148#post928148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>That</i> is scary. And the Game of Thrones reference is a nice one. Now, I am starting to imagine the Lodge being like some sort of Werewolf Faceless Men thanks to it.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My work here is done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=928148#post928148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of dot rating, perhaps that Rite would be a five-dot one? I can see it being used effectively as a form of punishment against those who offended/harmed the Lodge in some manner. And it definitely would reinforce the significance of its adherents collecting the True Names of others, including the Awakened who are their sacred prey. Not to mention emphasize how steep a price one must pay to call on their services.</div> </div> </div> </div>5 dots sounds about right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T09:10:42-07:00","id":928190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=928148#post928148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a similar note, the Rite would most certainly be the greatest act of devotion that true faithful of <i>Humuz-Ur</i> could demonstrate. And such werewolves are perhaps merely extensions of their Totem's will as well as her favored vessels once they've made that sacrifice. It could be even possible that we could design a lesser Rite that could somehow harness the True Names given to the Firstborn, which could function similarly to the Masque Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Combine that with the Face-Stealing Gift, and it gets really scary.<br /> <br /> Would a Rite that lets them learn the name of a slain foe be appropriate (and thus, lets them assume their identity and Sympathetic Connections, as per options above)? Or &quot;force&quot; the Eater to learn their foe's name before the end?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T09:20:48-07:00","id":928199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=928190#post928190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Combine that with the Face-Stealing Gift, and it gets really scary.<br /> <br /> Would a Rite that lets them learn the name of a slain foe be appropriate (and thus, lets them assume their identity and Sympathetic Connections, as per options above)? Or &quot;force&quot; the Eater to learn their foe's name before the end?</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason, I imagine that would require the Eater to <i>eat</i> the flesh of his foe, and thus force a Breaking Point. And I imagine that such a Rite would be appropriately called the &quot;Feast of Names&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T12:58:33-07:00","id":928359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=928199#post928199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For some reason, I imagine that would require the Eater to <i>eat</i> the flesh of his foe, and thus force a Breaking Point. And I imagine that such a Rite would be appropriately called the &quot;Feast of Names&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given most Uratha only need a taste of their quarry's blood to know where they are at all times, I imagine that's enough of a symbol for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T17:28:46-07:00","id":928523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=928190#post928190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Rite that lets them learn the name of a slain foe be appropriate (and thus, lets them assume their identity and Sympathetic Connections, as per options above)? Or &quot;force&quot; the Eater to learn their foe's name before the end?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably unnecessary, definitely way under-powered. There's a Gift 'Know Thy Prey,' with a regular success, 'The Uratha immediately knows every name that the prey is known by, as long as someone else other than the prey knows it. He also knows any Alternate Identity or Fame Merits that the target possesses. In addition, he becomes aware of every Allies, Contacts, Retainer, Resources, Staff, and Status Merit that the target possesses with equal or fewer dots than successes rolled.'<br /> <br /> It is not even contested or resisted, though the dicepool is penalized by an Anonymity merit, and can be used on anyone the werewolf perceives that is present. Any Uratha with 1 Honor Renown can get it.<br /> <br /> Think more powerful. More hunter. <br /> <br /> Rites would be based on ancient pacts forged between spirits and Other Things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-08-2016, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T05:50:46-07:00","id":928703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=928523#post928523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably unnecessary, definitely way under-powered. There's a Gift 'Know Thy Prey,' with a regular success, 'The Uratha immediately knows every name that the prey is known by, as long as someone else other than the prey knows it. He also knows any Alternate Identity or Fame Merits that the target possesses. In addition, he becomes aware of every Allies, Contacts, Retainer, Resources, Staff, and Status Merit that the target possesses with equal or fewer dots than successes rolled.'<br /> <br /> It is not even contested or resisted, though the dicepool is penalized by an Anonymity merit, and can be used on anyone the werewolf perceives that is present. Any Uratha with 1 Honor Renown can get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for pointing that out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=928523#post928523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think more powerful. More hunter.<br /> <br /> Rites would be based on ancient pacts forged between spirits and Other Things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of Rites, working on that five-dot one Vent0 suggested. But it's still a WIP.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Feast of Names</u> (ooooo)<br /> <br /> Symbols: </b>Connections, Endings, Humuz-Ur, Sacrifice, True Name<br /> <b>Cost: </b>5 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> <br /> <b>Duration: </b><br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T03:55:40-07:00","id":929649,"title":"","content":"Having a bit of a block on working out that &quot;Feast of Names&quot; Rite, as well as a write-up for the Eaters of Names as a Lodge. In the meantime, though, here's another Lodge concept that sprung from my brainstorming for Age of Azar content. This one is also a work in progress, but the idea here is that it's a true Sun-worshipping Lodge as opposed to the Temple of Apollo and its alien Totem. In Age of Azar (which is an expansion of the Cannibal Hymn''s setting), this sect is tied to an extent with the mortal solar priesthood. However, since sun worship is found among other ancient cultures, it shouldn't be too hard to create regional variations for other parts of the world.<br /> <br /> I still got nothing, though, on the Totem for this Lodge. Part of me was somehow thinking of using the Incandescent (or Opalescent?) Twins, Firstborn who commanded Uratha and humans to raise up temples to Helios during the time of the Sundered World. Right now, though, I am thinking of settling for a Hellion of Rank 4 or 5 being their patron instead. Feel free to air your thoughts on this. <hr /><br /> <u><b>The Sun Walkers</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>TOTEM:</b> ???? ????<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>BOND</b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Lodge member regains a point of Essence for every hour spent under the sun. In addition, most Hellions have at least average or good first impressions towards him for the purpose of Social Maneuvering.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To accomplish a task for a high-ranking Hellion.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> To fulfill all oaths sworn before a Hellion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>SACRED HUNT</b><br /> The Sacred Hunt grants your character greater prowess as a tracker under Helios' light. Any tracking rolls made to track prey during the hours of the day gain an Exceptional Success at three successes instead of five. Furthermore, the Perception bonuses of a Lodge member's forms are increased by +1 during this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T05:20:19-07:00","id":929667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=929649#post929649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still got nothing, though, on the Totem for this Lodge. Part of me was somehow thinking of using the Incandescent (or Opalescent?) Twins, Firstborn who commanded Uratha and humans to raise up temples to Helios during the time of the Sundered World. Right now, though, I am thinking of settling for a Hellion of Rank 4 or 5 being their patron instead. Feel free to air your thoughts on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with a Hellion. No need to throw more Firstborn into the picture unless you have to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=929649#post929649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blessing:</b> The Lodge member regains a point of Essence for every hour spent under the sun. In addition, most Hellions have at least average or good first impressions towards him for the purpose of Social Maneuvering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this <i>really</i> powerful? They don't even need Loci if they have this. Maybe 1 Essence per day (or 8 hours) spent in sunlight? This lets them accumulate Essence over time, if needed, while still making Loci have some value. Or maybe treat &quot;anywhere in sunlight&quot; as a \u2022 Locus?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=929649#post929649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Aspiration:</b> To accomplish a task for a high-ranking Hellion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=929649#post929649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ban:</b> To fulfill all oaths sworn before a Hellion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are Oaths really important to them? What about to never treat with Helios's enemies, or to only hunt during the day?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=929649#post929649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>SACRED HUNT</b><br /> The Sacred Hunt grants your character greater prowess as a tracker under Helios' light. Any tracking rolls made to track prey during the hours of the day gain an Exceptional Success at three successes instead of five. Furthermore, the Perception bonuses of a Lodge member's forms are increased by +1 during this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't there Merits or Gifts that already grant these kind of Perception and Tracking bonuses?<br /> <br /> What about knowing the location (in general or specific) of the Prey, as long as they are in view of the Sun?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T06:28:16-07:00","id":929683,"title":"","content":"Re: Sacred Hunt - Give them Prey's Blood as long as the prey is under sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T06:39:15-07:00","id":929691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=929667#post929667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go with a Hellion. No need to throw more Firstborn into the picture unless you have to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. And now, I just need to work out the details of this Hellion, like how powerful it is (Rank 4 or 5?), and what its relation to the Sun Walkers is like. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=929667#post929667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't this <i>really</i> powerful? They don't even need Loci if they have this. Maybe 1 Essence per day (or 8 hours) spent in sunlight? This lets them accumulate Essence over time, if needed, while still making Loci have some value. Or maybe treat &quot;anywhere in sunlight&quot; as a \u2022 Locus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. 1 Essence per hour <i>does</i> seem to be too much. I'll probably go with the daily interval. How about the improved First Impression with Hellions aspect? Is it fine?<br /> <br /> Here's the revised write-up.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Lodge member gains a point of Essence the first time he sees the sun in a day. In addition, most Hellions have at least average or good first impressions towards him for the purpose of Social Maneuvering.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=929667#post929667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Oaths really important to them? What about to never treat with Helios's enemies, or to only hunt during the day?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having a hard time choosing between those two.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=929667#post929667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't there Merits or Gifts that already grant these kind of Perception and Tracking bonuses?<br /> <br /> What about knowing the location (in general or specific) of the Prey, as long as they are in view of the Sun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like this?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>SACRED HUNT</b><br /> The Sacred Hunt allows your character to unerringly track prey within Helios' sight. So long as they are in the view of the sun, the werewolf may sense his general direction as if he has tracking him through his blood. If he <i>does</i> actually taste his prey's blood, he is aware of his exact location so long as he is in a location touched by sunlight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T07:16:00-07:00","id":929711,"title":"","content":"Given the Sun requirements so far, I'm thinking they would <i>really</i> hate vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T08:56:50-07:00","id":929765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=929711#post929711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the Sun requirements so far, I'm thinking they would <i>really</i> hate vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. Though they can probably still get to them through their ghouls and blood dolls. And even then, I imagine Kindred wouldn't be too keen on trying to antagonize a Lodge patronized by a <i>sun spirit</i> of all things. In Age of Azar's setting, though, perhaps the Bak-Ra Bloodline might have a little better luck on cultivating ties with the Sun Walkers. Or maybe they'd be despised even more by the Lodge compared to other vampires.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, would the Sun Walkers have access to the same Lodge Merits as the Temple of Apollo? Connections, Sorcery, and Stronghold? If they can purchase Lodge Sorcery, we can probably swap Hunger out for something more appropriate to a Hellion Totem. What that new Influence could be, though, is something I haven't fully worked out. And would the Hellion itself work as a Rank 5 spirit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T11:06:08-07:00","id":929839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=929765#post929765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely. Though they can probably still get to them through their ghouls and blood dolls. And even then, I imagine Kindred wouldn't be too keen on trying to antagonize a Lodge patronized by a <i>sun spirit</i> of all things. In Age of Azar's setting, though, perhaps the Bak-Ra Bloodline might have a little better luck on cultivating ties with the Sun Walkers. Or maybe they'd be despised even more by the Lodge compared to other vampires.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, would the Sun Walkers have access to the same Lodge Merits as the Temple of Apollo? Connections, Sorcery, and Stronghold? If they can purchase Lodge Sorcery, we can probably swap Hunger out for something more appropriate to a Hellion Totem. What that new Influence could be, though, is something I haven't fully worked out. And would the Hellion itself work as a Rank 5 spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For a Lodge Totem, I'd be inclined to go with Rank 5, provided they are fairly widespread and not niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T11:11:32-07:00","id":929843,"title":"","content":"The totem spirit of a Lodge is always at least Rank 2. Most are Rank 3 or greater, with Rank 2 totems occurring when a once-powerful spirit has weakened from its former stature.<br /> <br /> What is the Sun Walker lodge about? What do they do that makes them different from regular werewolves or the Lodge of Apollo? Because building temples seems to be what the Temple of Apollo is about. It's so much about them that they have it in their name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T18:54:36-07:00","id":930099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=929839#post929839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a Lodge Totem, I'd be inclined to go with Rank 5, provided they are fairly widespread and not niche.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, seeing as sun worship isn't only prevalent in Egypt (especially during the First Turn), but also in other parts of Africa and beyond, I'd say it should be somewhat widespread.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=929843#post929843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The totem spirit of a Lodge is always at least Rank 2. Most are Rank 3 or greater, with Rank 2 totems occurring when a once-powerful spirit has weakened from its former stature.<br /> <br /> What is the Sun Walker lodge about? What do they do that makes them different from regular werewolves or the Lodge of Apollo? Because building temples seems to be what the Temple of Apollo is about. It's so much about them that they have it in their name.</div> </div> </div> </div>My concept for the Sun Walkers is that they are <i>Uratha</i> who turned away from Luna in order to gain the favor of Helios as their guardian. Admittedly, it's still a concept that needs more development (like the Eaters of Names), but I felt it would be nice to explore the idea of a Lodge which has an affinity for the Hellions that's <i>much more genuine</i> than that of the Temple of Apollo, and still cleaves to the philosophies of the Forsaken (or Pure) in its beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T19:43:57-07:00","id":930129,"title":"","content":"I don't see how they could turn away from Luna and still cleave to the philosophies of the Forsaken. That's much more readily a Pure concept.<br /> <br /> You might want to boil down what these werewolves do. Helios isn't really expanded upon much in the books and his second edition incarnation doesn't like werewolves so he, or his helion, would likely be demanding a lot and taking a lot in return. You might find it easier to fill in the rest of things when you get that foundation going. A totem is going to be a heavy influence on a lodge, and even the ones that cling to the Firstborn and Secondborn are strange sects with weird practices.<br /> <br /> Incidentally while I appreciate that the Apollo creature isn't Helios, I always thought it was linked heavily to Incandescence, for the similarities in motives. A Firstborn that had to find another way to survive and was, consequently, locked out of Earth's Hisil by Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T22:46:07-07:00","id":930181,"title":"","content":"I actually think it's a great concept for a Pure lodge. Perhaps Firetouched. With the goal of wanting to replace their ties to Luna by tying themselves to Helios instead. Or perhaps to exalt a powerful Helion (lodge totem) in Helios' place. I had a similar idea for a Pure character I played who was a former Cahaltih who had torn out his auspice due to his sensitivity to Luna's visions and the pain/madness they had begun to cause in him. He suffered a crisis of faith, and sought to replace Luna's madness with Helios' steadfast reliability.<br /> <br /> Like you said, probably a very harsh and demanding totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T07:14:46-07:00","id":930315,"title":"","content":"Agreeing that if they turned away from Luna for Helios, they definitely sound more Pure than Forsaken. Would they be loosely affiliated to one of the existing Tribes, have multiple representations/relations, or be apart form the larger Tribal structures?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T07:33:05-07:00","id":930323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=930315#post930315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreeing that if they turned away from Luna for Helios, they definitely sound more Pure than Forsaken. Would they be loosely affiliated to one of the existing Tribes, have multiple representations/relations, or be apart form the larger Tribal structures?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine they'd have their origins with the Fire-Touched, given they are the Pure with the most affinity to the Shadow. And even by the standards of the Tribe, the Sun Walkers would be regarded as an extremely zealous Lodge. After all, no fire in the World of Flesh is greater or purer than that of the Sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T03:53:16-07:00","id":935506,"title":"","content":"More ideas thought up for my soon-to-be-posted Sun Walkers thread. <hr /><br /> <u><b>TOTEM: The Eye of Providence</b></u><br /> The Hellion who bestowed its favor upon the Sun Walkers is a powerful spirit that demands much for its patronage. It manifests as a living mandala of fire and light, and it can easily scorch everything in its presence with a mere thought. Those who fall under its gaze are struck with a sense of awe and fear, and even the most devout adherents can't help but feel unclean whenever it appears before them.<br /> <br /> Werewolves claimed by the Eye stand out from their fellow Tribesmen. Their Renown does not glow with the blood red hue of the Pure. Instead, they blaze with golden fire, and it is said that those who touch them in the Hisil quickly pull away when they feel their hands burn. Other signs of the Hellion's influence can be seen in both their great fervor, and the sense of aversion they get whenever they are touched by the Moon's light.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the Eye of Providence holds great hostility towards spirits of the lunar choirs. It expects its werewolves to slay Lunes as proof of their loyalty to Helios. As a result, Sun Walkers routinely conduct the Sacred Hunt in order to offer at least one Lune for each phase of the moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T12:09:54-07:00","id":935732,"title":"","content":"I love the idea behind this one. I like anything that incorporates more Helions into the setting. Though, I would really like to know more about the totem's motives.<br /> <br /> Like, how does Helios feel about this cult? He's likely indifferent or ignorant of it, of course, but how would he feel? From what I remember, Helios hates the Children of Luna, but not Luna herself. She is his sister, afterall. So is this a rogue Helion, masquerading as a representative? A blasphemous helion ousted from the choir? Is it a Helion using the increased power and influence of being totem to maybe subvert or one day supplant Helios? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T21:56:04-07:00","id":935939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=935732#post935732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the idea behind this one. I like anything that incorporates more Helions into the setting. Though, I would really like to know more about the totem's motives.<br /> <br /> Like, how does Helios feel about this cult? He's likely indifferent or ignorant of it, of course, but how would he feel? From what I remember, Helios hates the Children of Luna, but not Luna herself. She is his sister, afterall. So is this a rogue Helion, masquerading as a representative? A blasphemous helion ousted from the choir? Is it a Helion using the increased power and influence of being totem to maybe subvert or one day supplant Helios?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are all interesting possibilities. Personally, I'd probably combine the first and the last suggestion together. But i can definitely see the second point coming true if/when Helios or another Hellion equal to the Eye in Rank and power realizes its intentions.<br /> <br /> Oh, and finally posted up the full-write up. Feel free to give it a look <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 07-23-2016, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T13:40:53-07:00","id":936700,"title":"","content":"Ideas on Lodges that need elaboration and refinement:<br /> <br /> A Lodge of intrepid explorers. Their hunt is for new vistas and territories - to see what no other werewolf has seen before.<br /> <br /> A Lodge of the Feast. Gourmands, cannibals, industrialists, and experimenters, they seek to feed on and extract Essence from a variety of sources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T15:35:00-07:00","id":937337,"title":"","content":"I kind of want to update the Lodge of the Lake, possibly detailing its unpleasant patron using the Idigam rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:03:50-07:00","id":938766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=936700#post936700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas on Lodges that need elaboration and refinement:<br /> <br /> A Lodge of intrepid explorers. Their hunt is for new vistas and territories - to see what no other werewolf has seen before.<br /> <br /> A Lodge of the Feast. Gourmands, cannibals, industrialists, and experimenters, they seek to feed on and extract Essence from a variety of sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lodge of the Endless Horizon (from <i>Signs of the Moon</i>) fills in the first idea. As for the second one, I think you should look at the Lodge of the same name in <i>Lodges: The Splintered</i>. At the very least, it might give some starting material for a 2E conversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:03:50-07:00","id":938767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=937337#post937337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of want to update the Lodge of the Lake, possibly detailing its unpleasant patron using the Idigam rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. On a related note, I'm actually interested in seeing a 2E guide for depicting the Maeltinet (and Maeljin) rules-wise. Plus, I was wondering if I could put together a write-up for a new Lodge that could supposedly have been organized by the former totem of the Lodge of the Lake?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 07-28-2016, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:27:36-07:00","id":938784,"title":"","content":"Y'know, that just hit me. Balehounds would fit perfectly as a Lodge with the new rules. Specifically just gaining a Blessing to hide among the Pure or Forsaken despite their markings being all kinds of fucked up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T05:36:37-07:00","id":939463,"title":"","content":"I've got ideas for another Tribal Pillar write-up. This time, it's the Lodge of Arms. However, I'm not quite sure whether or not the 1E Totem is applicable for them. Not to mention I have no idea how to write their Aspiration and Ban. Anyway, here's what I got. <hr /><br /> <u><b>BOND</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Lodge member gains the 8-Again quality on all rolls to craft, study, or use weapons.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspiration: </b><br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>SACRED HUNT</b></u><br /> The Lodge Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to assess his prey's combat skills. At a glance, he may determine his dots and Specialties in the following Skills (Athletics, Brawl, Firearms, and Weaponry), as well as any Fighting Style Merits he has invested in.<br /> <br /> <u><b>TOOLS</b></u><br /> Lodge members may purchase the Lodge Armory, Lodge Connections, and Lodge Stronghold Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T05:53:37-07:00","id":939473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=938784#post938784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'know, that just hit me. Balehounds would fit perfectly as a Lodge with the new rules. Specifically just gaining a Blessing to hide among the Pure or Forsaken despite their markings being all kinds of fucked up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still prefer them as a tribe. With outliers from pact-makers and Maeljin loyalists acting within the tribes per usual. There's no mention of their Renown brands being any different from anyone else's in first edition. Lunes seem to care about the act, not your personal beliefs, which is why Ghost Wolves still get Renown.<br /> <br /> Plus they have an active Firstborn and seem like something that would have been around more and be more relevant and numerous than the Eaters of the Dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-29-2016, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T21:52:55-07:00","id":960232,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to convert the Lodge o the Saviour to Second Edition, does someone has some ideas?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><u><b>BOND</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> \u00bf?<br /> <br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Bring the salvation of Our Lord Jesus Christ to other werewolves.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Never Hunting good christians?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>SACRED HUNT</b></u><br /> ?????<br /> <br /> <u><b>TOOLS</b></u><br /> Lodge members have access to the Blood Rosary Fetish (o)<br /> They also have access to the Lodge Merits: Connections (limited t christian churches or organizations) and \u00bfSorcery? \u00bfLorehouse?<br /> May be some rite related to church rites and Sacraments (as a Uratha version of Eucharisty or some rite of Confession who helps to resist Harmony breaking points or to recover Harmony)?</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T00:56:29-07:00","id":960285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=960232#post960232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to convert the Lodge o the Saviour to Second Edition, does someone has some ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Blessing:</b> Redeemers gain a +3 bonus when resisting the Influences, Manifestations, and Numina of ephemeral entities. They also benefit from the 8-again rule whenever they are targeted by spirit servants of the Maeljin.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> As for the Sacred Hunt blessing, perhaps it could offer benefits against Wounds and the twisted Essence they produce if their Sacred Prey happen to be/include Maeltinet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T09:37:54-07:00","id":960499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=960232#post960232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to convert the Lodge o the Saviour to Second Edition, does someone has some ideas?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><u><b>BOND</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> \u00bf?<br /> <br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Bring the salvation of Our Lord Jesus Christ to other werewolves.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Never Hunting good christians?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>SACRED HUNT</b></u><br /> ?????<br /> <br /> <u><b>TOOLS</b></u><br /> Lodge members have access to the Blood Rosary Fetish (o)<br /> They also have access to the Lodge Merits: Connections (limited t christian churches or organizations) and \u00bfSorcery? \u00bfLorehouse?<br /> May be some rite related to church rites and Sacraments (as a Uratha version of Eucharisty or some rite of Confession who helps to resist Harmony breaking points or to recover Harmony)?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Make the ban something like &quot;Never desecrate the house of the Lord&quot;, meaning prey can find refuge in places of worship to the Abrahamic God.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they take vows of chastity.<br /> <br /> That aspiration would need some means by which to accomplish it. What is the lodge's prey? Bale Hounds? The Sacred Hunt Blessing could make the immune to the effects of Wounds.<br /> <br /> I like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a>'s suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-30-2016, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T11:00:43-07:00","id":960550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=960232#post960232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to convert the Lodge o the Saviour to Second Edition, does someone has some ideas?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><u><b>BOND</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> \u00bf?<br /> <br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Bring the salvation of Our Lord Jesus Christ to other werewolves.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Never Hunting good christians?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>SACRED HUNT</b></u><br /> ?????<br /> <br /> <u><b>TOOLS</b></u><br /> Lodge members have access to the Blood Rosary Fetish (o)<br /> They also have access to the Lodge Merits: Connections (limited t christian churches or organizations) and \u00bfSorcery? \u00bfLorehouse?<br /> May be some rite related to church rites and Sacraments (as a Uratha version of Eucharisty or some rite of Confession who helps to resist Harmony breaking points or to recover Harmony)?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'd suggest starting by figuring out who the Lodge's totem is and what they want, as well as why the Lodge hunts what it hunts. Everything else cascades off of those two things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T11:35:16-07:00","id":961132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=960550#post960550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI'd suggest starting by figuring out who the Lodge's totem is and what they want, as well as why the Lodge hunts what it hunts. Everything else cascades off of those two things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totem Ideas for the Lodge of the Savior:<br /> Lupus Dei (Wolf of God) whom demands his followers Sacred Hunt those <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nI8OtOfzUDE\" target=\"_blank\">that do great evil in the name of the God</a> of Jacob and Esau, the one whom begot Jesus Christ (The Judaeo-Christian God whom Islam claims Muhammad was his prophet).<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Also the Creatures of Sin suggestion below is a clear path that would fit the Good vs Evil narrative most people understand about morality. I do like the idea and hit that like button. The reason I don't abandon my suggestion for the Sacred Hunt is that Salvation is a gift of divine grace for all are creatures disposed towards selfishness and evil in a Fallen World. The linked commandment properly translated and put in context (the opposite of semantic game playing with modern definitions done with a scoffing heart) is a theological place where Matthew 5:29, Mark 9:47, with its metaphor of the Church as a body and certain members doing evil or leading others towards evil meets a place where the idea of the Sacred Hunt could find theological footing amid a sea of doctrines of mercy. Evil done in the name of God is a strong force driving up forsaking of the concept of God. Bonus it subverts the Good vs Evil Narrative in exchange for &quot;the failure of authority (moral authority in this case) to police its own is what undermines authority the most&quot; which is trend in western media coverage.<br /> <br /> I think both ideas are strong candidates, , maybe a broader category of &quot;Those that war against the Image of God&quot; which would include creatures of sin and those attacking the Image of God by those doing evil in the name of God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-31-2016, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T11:41:47-07:00","id":961135,"title":"","content":"I mean, they already had a Totem. Not much of one, but maybe some work can be done to flesh out &quot;The Image&quot;? <br /> <br /> As for prey, maybe something like &quot;Creatures of Sin&quot;, representing Bale Hounds, Wound Spirits, and other beings who have objectively let vice become a part of their beings (like, say, the demons and Possessed of the Inferno suplement)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:05:45-07:00","id":961149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=961135#post961135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, they already had a Totem. Not much of one, but maybe some work can be done to flesh out &amp;quot;The Image&amp;quot;? <br /> <br /> As for prey, maybe something like &amp;quot;Creatures of Sin&amp;quot;, representing Bale Hounds, Wound Spirits, and other beings who have objectively let vice become a part of their beings (like, say, the demons and Possessed of the Inferno suplement)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Fleshing out more details on the Image is a good idea, given how Lodge Totems are more invested in their adherents.<br /> <br /> I definitely second &quot;creatures of sin&quot; as the Sacred Prey. We can also include Slashers into that category, and perhaps even the Shuankhsen and (low Integrity) Heroes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:15:05-07:00","id":961155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=961149#post961149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. Fleshing out more details on the Image is a good idea, given how Lodge Totems are more invested in their adherents.<br /> <br /> I definitely second &quot;creatures of sin&quot; as the Sacred Prey. We can also include Slashers into that category, and perhaps even the Shuankhsen and (low Integrity) Heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I'd try to keep it more focused actually. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3514\" data-vbnamecard=\"3514\">ZealousChristian24</a>'s idea about limiting/identifying it with creatures of Vice makes it nice and clear, without reading too much into things. Maybe let them do something toward beings that satisfied their Vice recently, as well? (That would inherently exclude most full template supernaturals, since they replace Vice as an Anchor. Demons and Mages, perhaps unironically, excepted)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T15:22:53-07:00","id":961266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=961149#post961149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely second &quot;creatures of sin&quot; as the Sacred Prey. We can also include Slashers into that category, and perhaps even the Shuankhsen and (low Integrity) Heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you base it on the seven sins? One would think breakers of the ten commandments or places of heathen worship would be more high priority for something so close to god. But then you might have to limit it to Ghost Wolves, what with the first.<br /> <br /> Why would the Image, or whatever totem, want sinners dead in sacred hunts?<br /> <br /> Basically are you trying to hold closer to religious belief? Or are you trying to make evil-smiting paladins?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-31-2016, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T06:21:06-07:00","id":967887,"title":"","content":"Thanks to all your suggestions. I really love the ban of &quot;Never desecrate the house of the Lord&quot;, and I think I'll use it.<br /> <br /> I liked the idea of Sacred Prey of: &quot;Those that war against the Image of God&quot;<br /> <br /> I also like the suggestion of &quot;Creatures of Sin&quot;, representing Bale Hounds, Wound Spirits..., but I think I'll use it for a Lodge I'm creating which is centered in battling the Bale Hounds.<br /> <br /> <br /> But, as <b>ZealousChristian24 </b>has said, the Lodge has a Totem, the Image, But It's poorly fleshed. I think I'll flesh it with more detail, following the suggestion of Acrozatariim. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the way, the context of my question is a detailed setting of Hunting Grounds: Spain.<br /> In my setting, a lot of local werewolves are very influenced by religion. Lodge of Saviour ihas a lot of influence, and also there's another one called Los Cruzados de Santiago (Crusaders of St. James) which is the most powerful and with most influence Lodge in Spain (I'll come later with it).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T08:22:20-07:00","id":967937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=960232#post960232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to convert the Lodge o the Saviour to Second Edition, does someone has some ideas?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><u><b>BOND</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> \u00bf?<br /> <br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Bring the salvation of Our Lord Jesus Christ to other werewolves.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Never Hunting good christians?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>SACRED HUNT</b></u><br /> ?????<br /> <br /> <u><b>TOOLS</b></u><br /> Lodge members have access to the Blood Rosary Fetish (o)<br /> They also have access to the Lodge Merits: Connections (limited t christian churches or organizations) and \u00bfSorcery? \u00bfLorehouse?<br /> May be some rite related to church rites and Sacraments (as a Uratha version of Eucharisty or some rite of Confession who helps to resist Harmony breaking points or to recover Harmony)?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Blessing Idea:<br /> Know Soul Dread Power, with things incapable of breaking points showing as &quot;Amoral or Immoral&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T22:31:48-07:00","id":968377,"title":"","content":"Some questions about a new Lodge 'm creating for a Spanish setting.<br /> <br /> Its name is &quot;Cruzados de Santiago&quot; (Crusaders of St. James) and was born during the Spanish Reconquista (the war of the christians kingdoms against the muslim kingdoms in Spain). Most of its members are spacially Storm Lords (in some regions, new Changed Storm Lords are initiated to the Tribe and to the Lodge at the same time, as if they were the same) and Blood Talons, although it has members of all tribes).<br /> <br /> Its patron spirit is the &quot;Sword of the Prophet&quot; (I've still have to translate its name to First Tongue), although it's mainly known among werewolves as the Sword of the Apostle. That's a reference of the legend of Santiago Matamoros (St. James Moor-slayer) who was one of the saints most venerated during the Reconquista (and today is the saint patron of Spain). Most Crusaders believe there's some relationship between their patron and the saint, but a few of them even identify it as the saint).<br /> <br /> Their patron was born as a small conceptual spirit of the Reconquista (a holy war spirit), who became the Totem of a pack. With time, after consuming conceptual spirits of Islam (as its prey) and other spirits of Reconquista, christian faith and war he grow until becoming the patron spirit of a lodge (its pack also had recruited other members to its cause, growing exponentially).<br /> <br /> With the pass of centuries, he continued growing until he became the Spirit of Spain, devouring other rivals during the process and the old spirit of Spain, who lost a lot of power after the muslim conquest. Today he's still the spirit of Spain, although he has rivals for that title. He represents the most traditional aspects of spanish culture (the most ultracatholic and conservative Spain), but in 19th century was born a rival candidate, la Dama Rep\u00fablica (Lady Republic), who is the spirit of the most progressive Spain. <br /> As there's been a constant ighting beteen those two ideas of Spain (&quot;las dos Espa\u00f1as&quot; -the two Spains-) in the last century between mostals, there's also been a combat of the conceptual spirits of those two ideas of Spain.<br /> As their patron spirit has increased in power, the Lodge also has become more and more important and powerful.<br /> <br /> Its concept is based in the Lodge of the Black Woods, from Lodges: The Splintered. It was very common initiate full packs as new members, and membership in the Lodge was not exclusive, accepting membership from other Lodges. My doubt is if with new Lodge rules, is still possible a Lodge who accepts membership from other Lodges (so those members will gain two blessings, Sacred Hunts, bans and Tools.<br /> If it's not possible in 2nd Edition, I've thought may be in an honorary membership for some sympatizer werewolves bit not fully-commited: acces to the tools, having to respect the ban and the aspiration, but without access to the blessing and Sacred Hunt benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T06:47:14-07:00","id":968487,"title":"","content":"I doubt they'd get the Blessing and Sacred Hunt benefit, but, as you suggested, they'd likely allow nominal participation in their ceremonies and freely trade merits and rites as long as they work out mutual trades and respect the views of the Lodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T07:03:48-07:00","id":968496,"title":"","content":"I think a lodge totem like that, especially one that seems so dedicated to loyalty and its belief over others wouldn't really put up with other lodges.<br /> <br /> It doesn't seem the most inclusive and accommodating of spirits. I suppose it might 'let' other lodges exist providing they offered up tithes, but I can't see it letting them in. Lodges are cults, the totems need loyalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T09:08:34-07:00","id":968556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=968377#post968377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My doubt is if with new Lodge rules, is still possible a Lodge who accepts membership from other Lodges (so those members will gain two blessings, Sacred Hunts, bans and Tools.<br /> If it's not possible in 2nd Edition, I've thought may be in an honorary membership for some sympatizer werewolves bit not fully-commited: acces to the tools, having to respect the ban and the aspiration, but without access to the blessing and Sacred Hunt benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is my understanding that werewolf Lodges are like vampire Bloodlines, changeling Entitlements, and mage Legacies in that members can only belong to one. I like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> 's suggestion of this lodge requiring tithes or tribute in areas where they are dominate. They seem very aggressive in their recruitment so dominating is likely unless they are likewise aggressively opposed.<br /> <br /> Three question: Why are they Stormlords instead Fire-Touched? Fire-Touched seem a very appropriate Tribe for the description you gave, more so than Stormlords. Are you creating this for Player Characters to participate in? Are you the storyteller or a player in the Chronicle these are meant to portrayed in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:40:46-07:00","id":968611,"title":"","content":"I also like the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> suggestion of Tribute and Tithe. I'd include that in a later rewritting.<br /> <br /> About your three questions, I'll begin with the two last ones because it helps to explain the others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=968556#post968556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you creating this for Player Characters to participate in? Are you the storyteller or a player in the Chronicle these are meant to portrayed in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither. I'm creating it as a macrosetting for all Spain. It'll be a big fan book about 500 or more pages. I wrote some years ago a similar setting for Spain vampires, and now I'm expanding it to werewolves. But although I haven't finished it, I'm also translating what I wrote to 2nd Edition rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=968556#post968556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are they Stormlords instead Fire-Touched? Fire-Touched seem a very appropriate Tribe for the description you gave, more so than Stormlords.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two reasons. The first one is that in the setting, religion has a strong influence in local werewolves. In modern days, not so much, but during the Reconquista against the moors, it was more important. Local werewolves participated in the Reconquista either helping christian armies or muslim. The truth is that most werewolves were fighting just for new territories, but the Reconquista was the religious and ideological excuse for attacking ther southern brothers. In fact, there is among Spanish Forsaken the (false) stereotype than the Reconquista was a war against Pure werewolves from muslim kingdoms (although the Pure only were dominant in the last centuries of muslim Spain, durin the Almohade and Almoravid invasions).<br /> Although most of Werewolves fought really for territorial conquests, there were a few faatical ones who really fought for religious reasons, the Crusaders of Santiago, who became allies with the Lodge of the Savior, in an alliance similar to the Church and nobility in the Middle Ages.<br /> <br /> The second reason is that when I created them first time, I followed the 1st Edition stereotype of the Storm Lords as the alfas of the alfas in Forsaken culture. With the change in 2nd Edition, I'll have to change that. I had stablished that the muslim werewolves were more tolerant with spirits than the christian ones. I'll probably remark that strongly, so there would be more Claimed in Muslim kingdoms than in Christian ones. So the Storm Lords were very interested in hunt them.<br /> <br /> Changing them to Fire-Touched would need a great setting change. But I also like your suggestion of them.I'm going to include a Middle Ages Lodge which rivalized with the Crusaders in Christian Spain, but who finally was defeated probably during the Castillian Civil Wars between Peter the Cruel and Henry of Trastamara (in fact, I have in the current setting an Ivory Claw who claims being descendant of Peter the Cruel).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 09-13-2016, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:25:35-07:00","id":968996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=968611#post968611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing them to Fire-Touched would need a great setting change. But I also like your suggestion of them.I'm going to include a Middle Ages Lodge which rivalized with the Crusaders in Christian Spain, but who finally was defeated probably during the Castillian Civil Wars between Peter the Cruel and Henry of Trastamara (in fact, I have in the current setting an Ivory Claw who claims being descendant of Peter the Cruel).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you could have a Pure off-shoot of original Lodge. Totem doesn't care on what side werewolves work for him...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T22:22:07-07:00","id":969025,"title":"","content":"Yes, in fact, I have something similar with a enemy Lodge from Catalonia, which inducts both Pure and Forsaken. In Barcelona (and, in a lesser extent, all Catalonia), there's a Lodge (Lodge of St George) who are the alphas in the region, and whose members are both Pure and Forsaken, in an antinatural coalition of both factions.<br /> <br /> EDIT: But yeah. I could go by your suggestion. But instead of being a lodge eith Pures and Forsaken working together for a common cause (as in Catalonia), in this case both would be deadly enemies. They even wouldn't know that their patron us the same (it would appear as a different to each Lodge).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 09-14-2016, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:05:40-07:00","id":974020,"title":"","content":"I have an idea for a lodge of thieves that foil plans that could harm their territory by stealing a critical component of that plan. It is inspired by a couple of stories out of new york city where terrorist bomb plots were inadvertently foiled when a thief either stole or attempted to steal the container the bomb was in, thus preventing it from going off (one of the stories (which may or may not be true) involves a pair of thieves that accidentally disabled one of the Chelsea bombs by stealing the fancy suitcase it was in and dumping the bomb out, which somehow disabled it, and the other one is a story where a car thief tried to steal a van, only to discover that the van was full of explosives and then called the police after moving the van to an abandoned waterfront area from the residential area it was in.).<br /> <br /> The idea may very well work better in demon, but if it were a lodge, I can't figure out what their blessing would be. I think their sacred hunt benefit would be being able to sense if their prey's plans (if any) is dependent on something material/stealable and being able to track that something as if it were the prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:24:02-07:00","id":974030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=974020#post974020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an idea for a lodge of thieves that foil plans that could harm their territory by stealing a critical component of that plan. It is inspired by a couple of stories out of new york city where terrorist bomb plots were inadvertently foiled when a thief either stole or attempted to steal the container the bomb was in, thus preventing it from going off (one of the stories (which may or may not be true) involves a pair of thieves that accidentally disabled one of the Chelsea bombs by stealing the fancy suitcase it was in and dumping the bomb out, which somehow disabled it, and the other one is a story where a car thief tried to steal a van, only to discover that the van was full of explosives and then called the police after moving the van to an abandoned waterfront area from the residential area it was in.).<br /> <br /> The idea may very well work better in demon, but if it were a lodge, I can't figure out what their blessing would be. I think their sacred hunt benefit would be being able to sense if their prey's plans (if any) is dependent on something material/stealable and being able to track that something as if it were the prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Going by the conversation in the Stranger Bedfellows thread (regarding the section of the same name in The Pack)... what about having a Demon <i>as</i> the Lodge's totem? Need to know a core component of a prey's plan? Heart's Desire Embed, or some Interlock or Lambda incorporating it.<br /> <br /> * For reference, the writer of the section was citing a Changeling as a possible Pack totem. If Changeling, why not Demon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:56:25-07:00","id":974045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=974030#post974030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. Going by the conversation in the Stranger Bedfellows thread (regarding the section of the same name in The Pack)... what about having a Demon <i>as</i> the Lodge's totem? Need to know a core component of a prey's plan? Heart's Desire Embed, or some Interlock or Lambda incorporating it.<br /> <br /> * For reference, the writer of the section was citing a Changeling as a possible Pack totem. If Changeling, why not Demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it, a demon that had such a lodge working for it probably also sometimes sends them to steal the lynchpins of certain GM plots, akin to the golden grin casino heist in payday 2. It creates a very nice crime.net sort of lodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:59:15-07:00","id":974047,"title":"","content":"That seems less like a lodge and more of a pack aligned with a demon.<br /> <br /> A lodge is a cult, with obedience and ritual and direction. This group is just protecting their territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:12:23-07:00","id":974056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=974047#post974047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems less like a lodge and more of a pack aligned with a demon.<br /> <br /> A lodge is a cult, with obedience and ritual and direction. This group is just protecting their territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're saying, and I am thinking the lodge would be an &quot;Across the western world&quot; thing, the totem has it's followers steal to protect their territory so that they can acquire wealth to pursue the totem's goals, which happen to align with theft and gaining influence in various organized crime groups.<br /> <br /> sort of a lodge of thieves dedicated to a totem representing the more romanticized thief.<br /> <br /> I am basically imagining Bain from the payday games as a totem for a lodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:50:22-07:00","id":974077,"title":"","content":"The stealing part is fine, it would make sense with a Magpie or simple Greed spirit, but 'to protect their territory' seems superfluous. Especially with the totem trying to gain influence in organized crime groups, which is an incredibly base goal. Becoming the King of Thieves seems like something a werewolf would do, not a lodge full of werewolves help their totem do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T20:10:14-07:00","id":974199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=974077#post974077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The stealing part is fine, it would make sense with a Magpie or simple Greed spirit, but 'to protect their territory' seems superfluous. Especially with the totem trying to gain influence in organized crime groups, which is an incredibly base goal. Becoming the King of Thieves seems like something a werewolf would do, not a lodge full of werewolves help their totem do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Organized crime is an ancillary benefit to their real goal of pulling off the biggest heist ever. (Insert Suitably Grandiose Target Here. Possible options: Stealing the whole world. If a Demon, stealing Command and Control of the God-Machine. Not one such named Infrastructure. <i>All of it</i>.)<br /> <br /> And what is a Lodge other than a bigger, older Pack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-21-2016, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T09:37:44-07:00","id":975557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=974199#post974199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Organized crime is an ancillary benefit to their real goal of pulling off the biggest heist ever. (Insert Suitably Grandiose Target Here. Possible options: Stealing the whole world. If a Demon, stealing Command and Control of the God-Machine. Not one such named Infrastructure. <i>All of it</i>.)<br /> <br /> And what is a Lodge other than a bigger, older Pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vent, I love your idea, stealing the GM itself would be a wonderful goal for a demon that became a lodge totem.<br /> <br /> I also have an idea for a lodge sponsored by a spirit of the mass media that hunts producers, writers, directors and actors in the movie, TV and (lately) video game industries whose projects threaten to upset the balance of power in the hisil by making millions of people think about a particular concept and flood it's related spirits with essence. The totem's goal is to control the media, thereby controlling what mortals think and through that controlling the hisil. The lodge's uratha just wants to keep Hollywood from messing up everyone's territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T09:04:37-07:00","id":977201,"title":"","content":"I thought I'd post a link to my Werewolf GMC/2nd ed hacks here. My Lodge conversions start on page 6 (above that are summary notes with a few tweaks and some 1st ed to 2nd ed merit conversions).<br /> <br /> Link: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/z2kw5s2\" target=\"_blank\">http://tinyurl.com/z2kw5s2</a><br /> <br /> Ok, back to your regularly scheduled conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T09:02:14-08:00","id":1043587,"title":"","content":"A question about the Sacred Prey of a Lodge I'm creating for my Spanish setting:<br /> <br /> <br /> The Circle of Trade:<br /> <br /> Originally called the Lodge of Sea, they were born in Middle Ages as a Lodge of Mediterranean Traders from the Crown of Aragon. They expanded for the Mediterranean thanks to the catalan Consulates of the Sea. In that time, the Lodge was centered on the sailor aspect over their tradesman aspect.<br /> With the &quot;discovery&quot; of the Americas, the Mediterranean lost its trade importance to the Atlantic Ocean, and the Lodge began a slow decadence to their near-extinction.<br /> <br /> In 19th Century, thanks to the Industrial Revolution, one of the few packs of the Lodge decided reinvent themselves. They centered more in the trader aspect over the sailor, and began a recreation of the Lodge as a trader's lodge mainly, with the sea element as a remainder of their past and their origins. So, the Lodge of Sea was reborn as the Circle of Trade.<br /> <br /> Their Patron was a Sea-Trade, a Mediterranean spirit centered in the rich mediterranean commerce during Middle ages. He preyed both trade and sea spirits, without becoming a magath (both aspects were definitory to them). With the reconversion of the Lodge of Sea in the Circle of Trade, he also began to prey more and more trade and money spirits over sea spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> Benefit: They don't suffer the effect of the climatic tilts if they're navegating in the Mediterranean, and when they are tradingthey require just 3 successes for an Exceptional Succes (alternatively, if players use the optional Social Maneuvering system, their First Impression is allways a level higher inthose cases).<br /> <br /> Aspiration: Gaining money.<br /> <br /> Ban: Never do anything for free. That includes helping Forsaken against the Pure, but in those cases, most Traders accept something symbolic as a payment just for not breaking the ban.<br /> <br /> But, which could be their Sacred Prey? I have an idea but I'm not sure if it could be possible:<br /> i they're going to do some trade with someone or some company, they call a Siskur-Dah in order to help them in busines: it could be a local generic Spirit, or may be (if you're trading ith some important company with a Shadow reflection) the spirit o that Company. It's not needed to kill the spirt, you just need to hunt him down and force him to use its Influence to help your business. If it's a generic trade Spirit, he gaves you a Repeat 9s quality. If it's the rival company spirit, it gives you the Repeat 8s quality.<br /> <br /> Could that be a viable Siskur-Dah?<br /> <br /> Thanks.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T03:45:13-08:00","id":1043907,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest coming at this from a different direction.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou have the broad idea - Mediterranean sea-wolves, with trade as their thing. Cool!<br /> <br /> \u200bNow figure out what it is they care about enough to refine their hunt over. Are they all dodgy heretics who believe it is necessary to 'balance the books' of the hunt, so they ensure that the prey or the prey's family always receives recompense for the loss of the victim? Do they find cultic ecstasy amidst the howling winds and foaming water of a storm at sea? Do they believe that the flow of wealth needs to be pure and uncontaminated, like the water of a river or a sea, so that life and prey can flourish - and therefore hunt those who would commit fraud or cheat or unsavoury hoarding of wealth that would choke off the flow of trade? Etc etc.<br /> <br /> \u200bOnce you know what they *care* about as a cult of hunters, then you can figure out the Siskur-Dah, and *then* things like Blessing/Ban/Aspiration should cascade off the back of that fairly easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T08:16:03-08:00","id":1043988,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your suggestions!!<br /> <br /> I'll use them to redefine de Lodge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: I had thought the last one (trade cheaters) also as a Sacred Prey, but I had failed to traslate it to a &quot;hunter language&quot;. I love your focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 02-05-2017, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T08:21:32-08:00","id":1043991,"title":"","content":"I just had a faint idea for a Lodge that could work for a crossover with Mummy.<br /> <br /> How do you envision a group of werewolves hunting after Seba? Or (if you want to widen their focus) Iremite Relics in general?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T08:34:02-08:00","id":1044001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1043991#post1043991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you envision a group of werewolves hunting after Seba? Or (if you want to widen their focus) Iremite Relics in general?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'd start by asking for the 'why' behind their desire to hunt those things, because 'we devour these ancient relics for power and to sate our ravenous hunger' is going to be a very different Lodge to 'these ancient relics are a taint on reality inflicted by an ancient and malevolent force, and must be excised'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T13:35:23-07:00","id":1070268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1044001#post1044001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI'd start by asking for the 'why' behind their desire to hunt those things, because 'we devour these ancient relics for power and to sate our ravenous hunger' is going to be a very different Lodge to 'these ancient relics are a taint on reality inflicted by an ancient and malevolent force, and must be excised'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might go for the latter, seeing as I have plans of making a Seba-based Legacy after getting a good look at the Mutapa chapter in the DE Companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T16:19:15-07:00","id":1073920,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to adapt the Fire-Touched Lodge of the Fevered Light (Blasphemies) to 2nd Edition. Their Patron is Fevered Dream (a spirit king of sickness) and the Lodge rules an human church as a cover for their activities (Im converting it in a Mystery Cult).<br /> My problem is that in 1st Edition, the Lodge gave as a benefit the Fever Gifts.<br /> <br /> I know Lodges cannot give affinity gifts, but it could be possible The Patron spirit court gave them access to those Fever Gifts (although with none afinity discount?<br /> <br /> Which benefits, sacred Prey, and Bans would you give them?<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T17:11:45-07:00","id":1073932,"title":"","content":"You could have a sacred hunt that opens up Fever Gifts as part of their initiation.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking about them too, but I didn't want to carry over the human church aspect. If I was converting it straight over I'd make their sacred prey 'the weak,' with a focus on those who are sick or diseased. As a ban accepting no healing from others seems to fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T17:25:15-07:00","id":1073936,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I love the idea of Fever Gifts as a part of their Sacred Hunt Initiaton. Your ban and Sacred Prey are almost the same I thought. And what about the Lodge general benefit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T17:40:00-07:00","id":1073943,"title":"","content":"I was thinking something like Acrozatarim's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1056100-lodge-of-the-seven-venoms-draft\">Lodge of Seven Venoms</a>, except with sickness and disease, as opposed to poison. Basically they become super carriers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T04:03:31-07:00","id":1074083,"title":"","content":"Instead of Fever gifts, Lodge sorcery (disease) is a good substitution I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T08:23:23-07:00","id":1074145,"title":"","content":"Yeah, its really a great idea that fits perfectly with the 2nd Edition style Lodges. I don't know how I didn't think on it before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T19:12:38-07:00","id":1075325,"title":"","content":"Lodge of the Grey Phoenix<br /> <br /> American Ivory Claw lodge that holds strong influence over the &quot;Still fighting the Civil war&quot; types in the South, I have a few ideas for it, but I want to get the Dark eras companion and it's reconstruction era before I write it up. I intend to have them allied with other villainous Neo-confederate z-splats from other supernatural types.<br /> <br /> Lodge blessing allows them to reach at all the Confederate memorials in the south as if they were loci<br /> <br /> They have access to the 3-dots lodge armory, two dot Lodge stronghold and any-dot lodge connections merits, except in the Atlanta area, where their secret base inside stone mountain gives them access to the 5-dot armory, 4-dot stronghold and 5-dot lorehouse merits in addition to the connections merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T00:28:59-07:00","id":1214455,"title":"","content":"Well, it's been nearly a year since this thread was last updated. But seeing as I'm picking up again my project of creating and converting Lodges, now is as good a time as any to bring it back.<br /> <br /> For starters, statting out Totems. Has anyone tried giving stats to the canon Totems we've had so far? Isim-Ur and Lycaon-Ur are the ones I'm most interested in seeing homebrewed stats for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T00:38:59-07:00","id":1214458,"title":"","content":"Well, Acrozatarim did a non-official take on Lycaon as a bodhisattva, didn\u2019t he?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T01:18:53-07:00","id":1214472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1214458#post1214458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Acrozatarim did a non-official take on Lycaon as a bodhisattva, didn\u2019t he?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did he? I don't recall seeing it. But on a related note, does it make sense that the Eater of Names is a Rank 5 spirit rather than Rank 6 like the major Firstborn if she (like Isim-Ur) is counted among her forgotten siblings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T01:34:16-07:00","id":1214477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1214472#post1214472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did he? I don't recall seeing it. But on a related note, does it make sense that the Eater of Names is a Rank 5 spirit rather than Rank 6 like the major Firstborn if she (like Isim-Ur) is counted among her forgotten siblings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lycaon-as-bodhisattva can be found on a thread called the Ultimate Predators or something. Don\u2019t recall the exact name. <br /> <br /> EDIT: It\u2019s \u201cAlpha Predators\u201d<br /> <br /> And I honestly have no idea about the Eater\u2019s appropriate Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 05-03-2018, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T01:39:23-07:00","id":1214480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1214477#post1214477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lycaon-as-bodhisattva can be found on a thread called the Ultimate Predators or something. Don\u2019t recall the exact name. <br /> <br /> EDIT: It\u2019s \u201cAlpha Predators\u201d<br /> <br /> And I honestly have no idea about the Eater\u2019s appropriate Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>Found it. Thanks.<br /> XD<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/798541-alpha-predators-the-strongest-werewolves?p=801351#post801351\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/798541-alpha-predators-the-strongest-werewolves?p=801351#post801351\"> Alpha Predators: The Strongest Werewolves - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/798541-alpha-predators-the-strongest-werewolves?p=801351#post801351\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/798541-alpha-predators-the-strongest-werewolves?p=801351#post801351 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Challenge: create a werewolf at the heights of werewolf power. Start with the basic character creation. You gain 45 Experiences to raise Primal Urge to 10. You have </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And yeah, finalizing on that Firstborn's Rank is really tricky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T04:24:46-07:00","id":1214524,"title":"","content":"With Urfarah being Rank 8, I'd personally have the eight main Firstborn be Rank 7 and minor Firstborn be Rank 6. The odds of a Rank 5 Pangaean/spirit surviving from the time of the Sundering or earlier has to be extremely low. Especially for those with a hunting nature that literally can't help stirring up shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T04:31:00-07:00","id":1214527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/921821-2e-lodges-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1214524#post1214524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Urfarah being Rank 8, I'd personally have the eight main Firstborn be Rank 7 and minor Firstborn be Rank 6. The odds of a Rank 5 Pangaean/spirit surviving from the time of the Sundering or earlier has to be extremely low. Especially for those with a hunting nature that literally can't help stirring up shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely taking a note of this, and not just for statting my version of the Eater of Names. I might have to revisit my writeup for Turtle so I can better reflect how he's the equal of Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T05:42:39-07:00","id":1214551,"title":"","content":"At least, that's my take for modern times. I'm guessing not much has changed for a while, but when getting closer to the advent of the Tribes I think the Firstborn would fluctuate in Rank.<br /> The &quot;minor&quot; Firstborn were probably not quite as forgotten by the Uratha and could've been Rank 7, or perhaps it was the tribal Firstborn that were Rank 6 before the Tribes became global phenomena and the constant flow of Essence through the tribal bond exalted them to Rank 7. Or a combination of both possibilities.<br /> At the time of the Sundering and earlier, I'd have all Firstborn be Rank 7 as they were directly born from Urfarah, and all Secondborn would similarly be Rank 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T22:36:39-07:00","id":1214920,"title":"","content":"Question - <b>Is Lodge Totem as <i>different</i> being than spirit a thing?</b> Because in <b>Beast Player's Guide</b> we have hint that Beast can be Lodge Totem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BPG, p. 135</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lodge of the Red Owl is dedicated to reverence and mastery of the hunt. The Final Peace serves as the de facto totem of an Iron Master pack, and teaches her human followers how to hunt with a werewolf\u2019s savage efficiency and cunning. Her flock\u2019s greatest calling is to pass these methods on to fellow hunters, even if that means making them prey first.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if that will be a case, so probably powerful ghosts, angels and other Ephemeral Beings could be also Totems in some weirder Lodges. I lately have idea of recasting my take on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge\">Valkyria Mot</a> into making it the Lodge serving powerful Underworld Kerberoi that looks very much as Odin. They are, in the end, from <b>Blasphemies</b> book... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T23:06:01-07:00","id":1214929,"title":"","content":"One of the first lodges mentioned in second edition, the Lodge of the Field, has a werewolf as a totem. And the 'Stranger Bedfellows' sidebar in the Pack further suggests you can have more out there things. Plus Apollo might not be a spirit either. So yeah it doesn't look like it's limited to spirits (everyone wants a piece of werewolf).<br /> <br /> But spirits (and perhaps werewolves) seem to gain the most from it, since most of the benefits are spirit related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-04-2018, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T23:10:32-07:00","id":1214931,"title":"","content":"What nofather said. I suspect the only real requirement to totem-hood is spiritual power, rather than actually being a spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}